::instructions

(pizza dough) <put, between (parchment paper)>
    <flatten, with (bottle), even if sold as super thin> ?= as thin as possible, 1-2mm, enough for two baking trays
    <place, on (baking trays)>
(oven) <preheat, 450-500°F / 230-260°C>
(cream) <spread, evenly over the dough, very thin layer barely covering it>
(onion) + (topping)
    <cut, into small pieces>
    <distribute, evenly over the dough>
{flammkuchen} <bake, in (oven), ~10m> ?= getting a little dark with thin parts browned
    <remove, from (oven)>
    <season, with (salt) + (pepper)>

::notes

The author usually removes it from the tray and cools it for 2-5 minutes before eating. Serve with a green salad.
Makes two large thin flammkuchen, one per person. Source dough link: /pizza-dough.
The source gives 150g for bacon but no amount for replacement vegetables.

::story

A recipe for Flammkuchen a very thin crust pizza-like dish - it originates from Elsass, a French region close to where I grew up. I like the recipe because it takes 10 minutes to prepare and another 10 minutes to bake. It goes well with a green salad as a side.


